From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 15:47:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] .15 Position State: required-vs-optional symbol
 handling for full coin universe

Same pattern as .13/.14: REQUIRED_SYMBOLS (BTC/ETH) remain the only
symbols whose absence or an invalid/inconsistent upstream risk decision
can block the whole position-state decision. Every other symbol .14
reports -- including one .14 itself individually blocked -- gets its own
position state independently.

Specific changes:
- verify_upstream()'s per-symbol loop scoped to REQUIRED_SYMBOLS only.
- New risk_decision_consistency_errors(symbol, item, allow_blocked) helper
  factors out the original per-symbol check; called with allow_blocked=False
  for the required-symbol gate (preserving exact prior behavior/reason
  strings) and allow_blocked=True per optional symbol, since an optional
  symbol may legitimately arrive BLOCKED from .14's own optional-symbol
  handling without that being a contract violation.
- build_position_state()'s main loop iterates every symbol .14 reported
  (union with REQUIRED_SYMBOLS): required symbols keep the original
  RISK_PASS->ENTRY_CANDIDATE / else->FLAT logic; optional symbols get
  ENTRY_CANDIDATE/FLAT/BLOCKED based on their own upstream decision,
  recorded in optional_symbols_blocked when BLOCKED, without affecting
  the required pair.
- overall_position_state now factors in ENTRY_CANDIDATE from ANY symbol
  (required or optional) -- consistent with .13/.14's existing
  any-symbol-can-signal design -- while an optional symbol's own BLOCKED
  state can never by itself flip the aggregate to BLOCKED.
- print_report() iterates actual decisions instead of a fixed BTC/ETH
  tuple, labeling each symbol REQUIRED/OPTIONAL.

Adds 9 contract tests, including optional-blocked-does-not-cascade and
an "only optional blocked, required flat -> overall FLAT not BLOCKED"
regression test. Also verified with a real .12-shaped snapshot run
through the actual .13 -> .14 -> .15 chain: a neutral BTC/ETH pair plus
an AVAX mirror-candidate signal reaches ENTRY_CANDIDATE, and a DOGE
symbol with invalid source data is cleanly BLOCKED at every stage without
affecting BTC/ETH/AVAX. Full suite (41 tests) green.

